load @term/seed/structure/ring
  find ring

# A ring, the concept: a set with addition and multiplication where addition is an abelian group and multiplication
# distributes over it. The integers are the first ring, and every rung of the number tower is one. The canonical ring
# form and its axioms are in the structure folder, and the machine-checked ring identities over the integers are in the
# number and polynomial files. This concept file marks the ring as a pillar of the algebra layer.
form ring-concept
  link structure, like ring
